<main id="main">

<section class="wm-hero"><div class="wm-w"><div class="wm-hero-g"><div><p class="wm-kick">The jacket guide for cold days</p><h1>Warmth is a choice you make before you leave the house.</h1><p class="wm-lead">Warmers is an independent guide to winter jackets. We explain insulation, fit and layering so you choose the right coat once, and stay comfortable all season.</p><p class="wm-acts"><a class="btn" href="#tools">Find my warmth level</a><a class="wm-ul" href="insulation-guide.html">Down vs synthetic &rarr;</a></p></div>
<aside class="wm-scale" aria-label="Temperature guide"><p>Quick scale</p><div class="wm-sc wm-sc1"><b>10&deg;C +</b><span>Light shell or fleece</span></div><div class="wm-sc wm-sc2"><b>0 to 10&deg;C</b><span>Light insulated jacket</span></div><div class="wm-sc wm-sc3"><b>&minus;10 to 0&deg;C</b><span>Mid-weight puffer or parka</span></div><div class="wm-sc wm-sc4"><b>Below &minus;10&deg;C</b><span>Expedition-weight down</span></div></aside></div>
<div class="wm-col"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1791233698988-8840ad8d449a?auto=format&fit=crop&w=700&h=460&q=75" alt="woman in a brown jacket and blue scarf in falling snow" width="700" height="460" fetchpriority="high"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1771074153183-5849e68c5da6?auto=format&fit=crop&w=360&h=460&q=75" alt="cream puffer jacket with fuzzy sleeves" width="360" height="460" fetchpriority="high"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1612617291435-fad1d935ec34?auto=format&fit=crop&w=360&h=460&q=75" alt="woman in a black jacket on a snowy road" width="360" height="460" fetchpriority="high"></div></div></section>

<section class="wm-s"><div class="wm-w wm-vs"><div class="wm-vs-i"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1769689387719-f11faac08cbe?auto=format&fit=crop&w=560&h=640&q=75" alt="man wearing a shiny black puffer jacket" width="560" height="640" loading="lazy"></div><div><p class="wm-kick">The big decision</p><h2>Down or synthetic?</h2><div class="wm-vs-t"><div><h3>Down</h3><ul><li>Warmest for its weight</li><li>Packs very small</li><li>Lasts many years with care</li><li>Loses loft when soaked</li></ul></div><div><h3>Synthetic</h3><ul><li>Stays warm when damp</li><li>Dries quickly</li><li>Easy to wash</li><li>Heavier and bulkier for the warmth</li></ul></div></div><p>Many modern jackets mix the two: down in the body, synthetic at the shoulders and cuffs where rain and sweat collect.</p></div></div></section>

<section class="wm-tl" id="tools"><div class="wm-w"><div class="wm-tl-h"><p class="wm-kick">Jacket tools</p><h2>Answer three questions, get a clear plan</h2></div>
<div class="wm-row"><div class="wm-row-n">I.</div><div class="wm-row-t"><h3>Warmth Picker</h3><p>Match a jacket to the weather and what you will be doing.</p></div><div class="wm-row-f"><label for="wp-t">Coldest temperature (&deg;C)<input id="wp-t" type="number" step="1" value="-2"></label><label for="wp-a">Activity<select id="wp-a"><option value="still">Standing or waiting</option><option value="walk" selected>Walking or commuting</option><option value="active">Hiking or cycling</option></select></label><label for="wp-w">Is it often wet?<select id="wp-w"><option value="0">Mostly dry</option><option value="1">Often damp or rainy</option></select></label></div><div class="wm-out" id="wp-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
<div class="wm-row"><div class="wm-row-n">II.</div><div class="wm-row-t"><h3>Jacket Size Helper</h3><p>Chest measurement plus what you wear underneath.</p></div><div class="wm-row-f"><label for="js-c">Chest (cm)<input id="js-c" type="number" min="70" max="150" step="1" value="98"></label><label for="js-l">Underneath<select id="js-l"><option value="0">T-shirt or shirt</option><option value="4" selected>Jumper or fleece</option><option value="8">Thick knit or two layers</option></select></label><label for="js-f">Preferred fit<select id="js-f"><option value="slim">Close</option><option value="reg" selected>Regular</option><option value="relax">Roomy</option></select></label></div><div class="wm-out" id="js-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
<div class="wm-row"><div class="wm-row-n">III.</div><div class="wm-row-t"><h3>Layer Builder</h3><p>Tick today&rsquo;s conditions to build an outfit from the skin out.</p></div><div class="wm-row-f wm-cks" id="lb-c"><label><input type="checkbox" value="cold" checked> Cold</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="wind"> Windy</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="rain"> Rain</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="snow"> Snow</label><label><input type="checkbox" value="active"> I&rsquo;ll be active</label></div><div class="wm-out" id="lb-o" aria-live="polite"></div></div>
</div></section>

<section class="wm-s"><div class="wm-w wm-fit"><div><p class="wm-kick">Fit check</p><h2>Five moves to test a jacket</h2><ol class="wm-moves"><li><b>Hug yourself.</b> The back should not pull tight across the shoulders.</li><li><b>Reach forward.</b> Cuffs should still cover your wrist bones.</li><li><b>Raise both arms.</b> The hem should not ride above your waist.</li><li><b>Zip to the chin.</b> The collar should close without pressing your throat.</li><li><b>Sit down.</b> A longer coat should not bunch or strain at the hips.</li></ol></div><figure><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1606808513294-e4cd2aa6124d?auto=format&fit=crop&w=520&h=620&q=75" alt="woman in a red jacket on a bridge" width="520" height="620" loading="lazy"></figure></div></section>

<section class="wm-s wm-oat"><div class="wm-w"><div class="wm-tl-h"><p class="wm-kick">In depth</p><h2>Two guides</h2></div><div class="wm-gds"><a href="insulation-guide.html"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1581056325587-d6c4020d4a0f?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=400&q=75" alt="person in a white jacket beside a snowy tree" width="640" height="400" loading="lazy"><div><span>Guide I</span><h3>The Insulation Guide</h3><p>Down, synthetic, fill power and fill weight, and how they decide real-world warmth.</p></div></a><a href="jacket-fit-guide.html"><img src="https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1548712370-806c729f72ef?auto=format&fit=crop&w=640&h=400&q=75" alt="man in a jacket leaning on a fence" width="640" height="400" loading="lazy"><div><span>Guide II</span><h3>The Jacket Fit Guide</h3><p>Measuring, sizing for layers, sleeve and body length, and the right fit for each style.</p></div></a></div></div></section>

<section class="wm-s"><div class="wm-w wm-fq"><div><p class="wm-kick">FAQ</p><h2>Cold-weather questions</h2><p class="wm-lead">Short answers to what readers ask us most often.</p></div><div class="wm-faq"><details open><summary>Down or synthetic insulation?</summary><p>Down is lighter and packs smaller for the same warmth, and lasts for many years with care. Synthetic insulation keeps more of its warmth when wet and dries faster, so it suits damp climates and high-sweat activities.</p></details><details><summary>What does fill power mean?</summary><p>Fill power measures how much space an ounce of down fills. Higher numbers, such as 700 or 800, mean loftier down that traps more warm air for its weight. It tells you about quality, not total warmth; that depends on how much down is used too.</p></details><details><summary>Should I size up for winter layers?</summary><p>Only if the jacket is cut slim. Try it on over the thickest layer you will wear. You should be able to cross your arms and reach forward without the back pulling tight.</p></details><details><summary>Is a waterproof jacket also warm?</summary><p>Not by itself. A waterproof shell blocks wind and rain, which helps a lot, but warmth comes from the layers underneath or from insulation built into the jacket.</p></details><details><summary>How do I wash a puffer jacket?</summary><p>Use a front-loading machine on a gentle, cool cycle with a down or technical wash, rinse twice, then tumble dry on low heat with a few clean tennis balls to break up clumps. Drying fully can take a few hours.</p></details><details><summary>Why does my jacket feel cold when it&rsquo;s wet?</summary><p>Water conducts heat away far faster than air and can flatten insulation. Keep the outer fabric&rsquo;s water-repellent finish topped up, and choose synthetic fill if you are often in rain.</p></details></div></div></section>

<section class="wm-nl"><div class="wm-w wm-nl-g"><h2>The Warmers Dispatch</h2><p>A short email each month through autumn and winter: one jacket explainer, one care tip.</p><a class="btn" href="mailto:hello@warmers.com?subject=The%20Warmers%20Dispatch&amp;body=Please%20subscribe%20me.">Subscribe by email</a></div></section>

